DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevX.11.041020","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc16R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1364\/OE.454493","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc17R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1209\/0295-5075\/92\/50010","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc18R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1364\/OSAC.1.000340","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc19R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.122.213901","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc20R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1364\/AOP.377940","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc21R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.108.043502","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc22R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/lpor.202402133","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc23R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.97.205422","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc24R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1364\/OE.443656","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc25R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevResearch.7.L012035","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc26R1","unstructured":"In his private communication to the author, Liu confirmed that the coupling theory [13] converges to the exact solution for the example in Fig.\u00a01, if each single-slab problem is treated purely numerically in a domain exceeding the coupled system, and all the numerical modes due to discretization and perfectly matched layers are taken into account.","type":"other"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc27R1","unstructured":"While the RSE in the presently available literature is not suitable for optical systems on a substrate, there is a prospect that such a geometry can ultimately be treated, for example, by extending the present approach to consider the substrate as a resonator coupled to the optical system.","type":"other"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc28R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.90.013834","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc29R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1364\/OL.43.001978","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc30R1","unstructured":"This is a harder case to address from the viewpoint of completeness, since otherwise the RSs of both systems would be complete in the overlap region without adding continua.","type":"other"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc31R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0375-9474(78)90488-8","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc32R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.87.043827","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc33R1","unstructured":"See Supplemental Material at http:\/\/link.aps.org\/supplemental\/10.1103\/fqzx-xtl9 for a full derivation of the analytical results of this Letter, optimization of the theory parameters f\u03b3 and fd, details on numerical calculation, more examples of coupled resonators and comparisons with the TMA, and a general theory of Casimir forces in terms of the RSs; includes Refs.\u00a0[13,15,17,18,20,25,29,32,34\u201349].","type":"other"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc34R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.94.235438","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc35R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.101.155128","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc36R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.95.115444","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc37R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.93.075417","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc38R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.85.023835","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc39R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.105.033522","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc40R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.134.103802","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc41R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.110.033518","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc42R1","volume-title":"Mathematical Methods for Physicists, 5th edition","author":"G.\u2009B. Arfken","year":"2001","type":"book"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc43R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.101.045304","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc44R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/cpa.3160030403","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc45R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.98.033820","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc46R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.101.053854","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc47R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.64.042102","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc48R1","volume-title":"Theory of Equilibrium Thermal Fluctuations in Electrodynamics","author":"M. Levin","year":"1967","type":"book"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc49R1","volume-title":"Statistical Physics, Part 2","author":"L.\u2009D. Landau","year":"1980","type":"book"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc50R1","unstructured":"A similar integration, though over a finite closed contour is used in the Riesz-projection theory [51].","type":"other"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc51R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.98.043806","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc52R1","unstructured":"For example, for a spherically symmetric resonator, s is a combination of the orbital and magnetric quantum numbers (l,m); for a planar system with mirror symmetry, s denotes even- and odd-parity states of the continuum.","type":"other"},{"key":"fqzx-xtl9Cc53R1","unstructured":"This concept may still be working for a subspace of infinite-Q modes, such as bound states in the continuum in coupled photonic-crystal resonators, as recently demonstrated in Ref.\u00a0[40].","type":"other"}],"container-title":["Physical Review Letters"],"original-title":[],"language":"en","link"